<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry IV of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1367">1367</a>–1413</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Henry Bolingbroke</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, Henry Bolingbroke, deposed his cousin Richard II in 1399 and founded the Lancastrian dynasty. His reign was spent putting down rebellions by the Percys and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr">Owain Glyndŵr</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>. In 1405 he granted the Isle of Man to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-stanley-died-1414">Sir John Stanley</a>, whose family ruled it as Kings and Lords of Mann for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-england.jpg" alt="Henry IV of England" width="320" height="382" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The National Archives UK · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illumination_of_Henry_IV_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
